## 9. Key Differences from Probability-Based Approach

| Aspect | Probability Approach | Qualitative Prompt Approach |
|--------|---------------------|----------------------------|
| Role transition | Weighted sampling from matrix | LLM reasons about "what's natural next" |
| Operation selection | Sample from role-specific weights | LLM selects based on role signature description |
| Shift calculation | Formula: ops_count + layer_bonus + platform_modifier | LLM assesses using qualitative rubric |
| Reviewer defensibility | "Why is Bridger→Amplifier = 0.53?" | "Patterns grounded in corpus observations" |
| Edge cases | Rigid (may produce implausible combos) | LLM can reason about unusual situations |
| Reproducibility | Higher (deterministic sampling) | Lower (LLM variance) — mitigate with temperature=0 |
| Hard constraints | Embedded in formulas | Separated into RuleGuard (minimal, absolute) |

